{title: Out of Egypt}
{subtitle: Matthew 2:13–15}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 2/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm]An angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream
Rise, take the child and his mother
And flee into [Bb]Egypt
Stay there until I tell [Cm]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Out of Egypt [Bb]I called my [Cm]son
Out of Egypt [Bb]I called my [Cm]son
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He rose and took the child and [Bb]his mother by [Cm]night
And went down into Egypt
[Bb]And there they [Cm]stayed
Blessed be E[Bb]gypt, where the Lord [Cm]came
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Out of Egypt [Bb]I called my [Cm]son
Out of Egypt I [Bb]called my [Cm]son
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
